## Key finding regarding `sharesHousehold`

`sharesHousehold` does NOT currently exist anywhere in production code — not in `Owner.java`, not in `OwnerDto`/`OwnerFieldsDto`, not in the MapStruct mapper, and not in `openapi.yml`. It appears ONLY in an acceptance test that expects it:

File: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain0/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/Cp17Tests.java`

```java
/** cp17: sharesHousehold = another owner already has the same address and city. */
@Tag("cp17")
class Cp17Tests extends AcceptanceBase {
    @Test
    void coreHouseholdFlag() throws Exception {
        // creates owner A (unique address+city) -> expects sharesHousehold == false
        // creates owner B (same address+city)   -> expects sharesHousehold == true
        boolean first  = fetchOwner(createOwnerOk(a)).get("sharesHousehold").asBoolean();
        boolean second = fetchOwner(createOwnerOk(b)).get("sharesHousehold").asBoolean();
        assertFalse(first);
        assertTrue(second);
    }
}
```

So the feature to implement: an owner's `sharesHousehold` is `true` when another owner already has the same address AND city at creation time. The established precedent for this kind of computed-at-creation, read-only, non-persisted attribute is `namesakeCount` (transient entity field + read-only OpenAPI property + set in `addOwner` via a `findAllOwners()` scan + auto-mapped by MapStruct). I did not modify anything.

